  "query_preview": "..\nRest of Today and Sunday: Widespread Red Flag conditions\ncontinue for much of the Inland Northwest today into early Sunday\nas a shortwave trough continues to race through the region. \nOverall, expect west- southwest winds around 10-20 with gusts \naround 18-25 mph in most locations under the Red Flag Warning. \nThe one exception will be the Cascade gaps where wind gusts in \nthe evening will be higher, generally around 25-40 mph. Fires in\nChelan and Okanogan County will be well ventilated with \nwesterly flow aloft and will have favorable weather conditions \nfor significant growth throughout the afternoon and evening \nhours. The smoke output from these fires may knock temperatures \ndown a few degrees in eastern WA and north ID and locations \nclose to the fire, reducing fire risk slightly. Needless to say,\navoid any activities that may cause sparks as fuels are near/at\nrecord dryness levels for this time of year. HRRR near surface \nsmoke output is still showing impressive concentrations this \nevening and overnight hours downwind in the eastern third of WA \nand north Idaho. If this were to occur, air quality will \ncontinue to degrade. Another push of Cascade gap winds will \noccur Sunday afternoon and evening as another shortwave \ntraverses the region, leading to once again, elevated to locally\ncritical fire weather conditions in the Wenatchee area and \nWaterville Plateau with gusts around 20-35 mph and relative \nhumidity around 18-25 percent. The wildcard is smoke reducing \ntemperatures in those areas, which would help with reducing fire\nrisk. \n\nMonday through Saturday: Zonal flow will continue through\nTuesday, bringing near normal temperatures and breezy winds to \nthe Cascade gaps in the evenings. There are some changes \non Wednesday as our first chance of precipitation in a few \nweeks returns near the Canadian border as a broad shortwave \ntrough approaches from the north. There continues to remain a \n10-20% chance of showers (with very little precipitation \nexpected) as this system moves through. There is a small chance \n(10-20%) of thunderstorms in northeast WA and north ID as this \nsystem slowly departs Thursday. Again, confidence is low in this\npattern but it is worth discussing since it'll be the first \nprecip chances in a while. Ensembles are hinting towards above \nnormal temperatures returning late next week but with troughing \nsetting up off the coast this raises concerns for thunderstorms.\n\n/DB-Mazurkiewicz",
